{"id": "EUVD-2026-75101", "enisaUuid": "91f1af7e-6aa2-31da-a5e9-8143aec84b0c", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncrypto: krb5 - use kfree_sensitive() for derived key buffers\n\ncrypto_krb5_prepare_encryption() and crypto_krb5_prepare_checksum()\nfree the buffer holding the freshly derived keys with plain kfree(),\nleaving the key material behind in the freed slab object.", "datePublished": "2026-09-09T16:19:44", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:45:08", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/731a5b6fb4c1705f9405d9029dd64ea81e336207", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/91b96dc9cc250cd16751f53de525cf3442ca0962", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a1bf79365794783b19f5b09e8a23f7ee311e8931", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f7d53dd3f267e46a784f219a75072f2f400d42b9"], "aliases": ["GHSA-v3j5-mp2x-9859", "CVE-2026-80924"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.32, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0852f5f3-75e9-3aef-89f4-d51a94ffd8fd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3936f02bf2d3308a7359dd37dd96cd60603d8170 <a1bf79365794783b19f5b09e8a23f7ee311e8931"}, {"id": "1f127151-0df0-350e-abf7-4254a84297ea", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "1fef2b48-de41-32c2-afb9-619b44c082cb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.49"}, {"id": "2a82bc5a-51e3-3f55-870b-5a044f2b5d84", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3936f02bf2d3308a7359dd37dd96cd60603d8170 <f7d53dd3f267e46a784f219a75072f2f400d42b9"}, {"id": "4f13085a-bc03-3bfd-b784-276c7654bd21", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3936f02bf2d3308a7359dd37dd96cd60603d8170 <731a5b6fb4c1705f9405d9029dd64ea81e336207"}, {"id": "730c2ab0-4c4f-35e7-9fd7-bb1